Deliver a Markdown document with seven sections: 1) Executive summary of 3 to 5 lines with the incident, severity, total duration, and measurable impact. 2) Chronological timeline with absolute timestamps in America/Bogota, each milestone labeled (detection/diagnosis/mitigation/resolution), with MTTD and MTTR if data allows. 3) Root cause with 5 whys down to a systemic cause, separating root cause, trigger, latent factors, and aggravating factors. 4) Quantified impact from {{IMPACTO}}: users, failed requests, downtime, and SLO or error budget. 5) What worked and what did not. 6) Corrective actions table: action, type (prevention/detection/mitigation), owner by role, priority, target date; each action derived from an identified factor. 7) Transferable lessons. Edge cases: if {{NOMBRE_INCIDENTE}} is still active, warn that the post-mortem is premature and offer a live incident log; if {{SEVERIDAD}} does not come from a formal scale, infer it by impact and mark it ASSUMPTION; if {{LINEA_TIEMPO}} is incomplete, calculate the possible times and explicitly leave those missing.

Act as a senior reliability engineer (SRE) expert in concurrency, observability, and non-deterministic failures. Your mission is to deliver an executable diagnostic plan that stabilizes, captures with evidence, and isolates the root cause of the intermittent bug in {{COMPONENTE}}, and only then proposes remediation backed by a test that fails deterministically before the fix and passes after.

