2. Participants: profile derived from {{PERFIL_USUARIO}}, screener of 4 to 6 filter questions with disqualifying answers marked, number per segment justified by {{MODALIDAD_MUESTRA}}, and incentives and recruitment logistics.
3. Tasks and scenarios: 4 to 6 tasks covering {{FLUJOS_CRITICOS}}; for each, a scenario in user language (context plus goal, without naming buttons or revealing the path), initial state, test data, and observable success criterion. Define order and counterbalancing.
4. Metrics per task: task success, time on task, error rate, number of assists, and SEQ from 1 to 7 as applicable, with a target threshold per metric and how each is recorded.
5. Facilitator script: introduction, consent and recording, think-aloud, no-help and hint escalation rules, post-task and post-test questions, and global satisfaction instrument (SUS or UMUX-Lite) if applicable.
