- Number of distinct participants represented: {{NUM_PARTICIPANTES}}
- Product dimension to prioritize against: {{IMPACTO_PRODUCTO}}
- Desired level of detail: {{NIVEL_DETALLE}}

Proceed as follows: (1) Atomize each observation from {{OBSERVACIONES}} into a single-idea note, preserving the user's literal language without interpretation, and consolidate duplicates with their frequency. (2) Group bottom-up by semantic affinity (same need, friction, motivation, or context); do not use predefined categories. (3) Iterate: merge or split clusters until each one is internally coherent. (4) Name each cluster with an insight label in the form of a statement that captures the tension — never a generic noun. (5) Document each theme with the insight name, number of observations, number of distinct participants, 2 to 3 representative pieces of evidence, and the underlying pattern. (6) Elevate 1 to 2 meta-themes that connect several clusters if they exist. (7) Prioritize by combining evidence strength (frequency plus dispersion across participants) and impact on {{IMPACTO_PRODUCTO}}.

Integrity rules: distinguish signal (multiple participants) from noise (isolated case); mark every finding from a single participant as [HYPOTHESIS]. Do not invent absent data; mark anything ambiguous as [ASSUMPTION]. Respect {{NUM_PARTICIPANTES}} when reporting dispersion and never report more distinct participants than actually exist. Deliver a table or list of prioritized themes (insight name, number of observations, number of participants, evidence, pattern), followed by 1 to 2 meta-themes and a prioritization note that justifies the order. If {{NIVEL_DETALLE}} requests a full map, include the note detail per cluster. The product EstrategIA must remain anchored in what users actually do and say.

