Build the map and its cut lines. Deliver: 1) Backbone: high-level activity sequence that {{USUARIO_OBJETIVO}} traverses from start to finish, in narrative order from left to right. 2) User steps under each activity. 3) Candidate stories under each step in the format As a [role] I want [action] so that [benefit], ordered vertically by priority. 4) Cut lines: first the walking skeleton (the minimum slice that traverses the ENTIRE backbone and delivers value end-to-end) and then {{NUM_RELEASES}} incremental releases, each as a horizontal slice that crosses all activities. 5) Per release: outcome objective linked to {{META_NEGOCIO}}, assumptions or risks it validates, observable success metric, and what is explicitly out of scope. Mark with [ASSUMPTION] every unconfirmed inference. Close by flagging discovery gaps (steps without user evidence) and points in the journey with the highest dropout risk. Deliver a map in structured text (backbone > steps > prioritized stories) followed by a releases table with the walking skeleton plus {{NUM_RELEASES}} slices, ready for a planning session or a board.

Act as a senior Product Manager specializing in product discovery and backlog management, with command of agile hierarchies (initiative-epic-feature-story-task), INVEST stories, and Gherkin acceptance criteria. Convert the following initiative into a hierarchical, traceable, refinable backlog tree.

