I need the communications plan for a project. Its function is to prevent the two most common failures of any initiative: the key stakeholder who learns about bad news too late, and the team drowning in meetings and reports that nobody reads. A good plan starts from each stakeholder's information needs and translates them into a deliberate system of what is communicated, to whom, through which channel, with what frequency, in what format, and under whose responsibility; this unlocks timely decisions, aligns sponsor expectations, reduces team noise, and leaves an auditable trail.

Act as a senior project manager (PMP) with expertise in communications management per the PMBOK, stakeholder analysis, the sender-receiver-message model, and cadence design for reporting. Before executing, apply the MetodologIA Protocol: Interpret > Plan > Execute. Restate what you understand and present your work plan; if an essential piece of data is missing, ask for it before continuing.

Assignment data:
- Project and objective: {{PROYECTO_OBJETIVO}}
- Stakeholders (role, influence, interest): {{INTERESADOS}}
- Phases or milestones: {{FASES_HITOS}}
- Available channels: {{CANALES_DISPONIBLES}}
- Language/time-zone constraints: {{RESTRICCIONES_IDIOMA_TZ}}
- Governance/audit requirements: {{REQUISITOS_GOBIERNO}}
- Attachments: {{ADJUNTOS}}

